<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 25,378,000 bushels -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 25,378,000 bushels -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 06/11/97    06/04/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 25,378,000  25,632,000    24,002,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  70,240	44,158	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   06/11/97    06/04/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,965,000   3,799,000     4,271,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,703,000   4,676,000     3,074,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,154,000   4,620,000     4,399,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,808,000   2,966,000     2,482,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,451,000   3,180,000     3,342,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,262,000   4,547,000     4,575,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,034,000   1,844,000     1,859,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	25,378,000  25,632,000    24,002,000</p>
